work/16-alex-hq/app/public/data/graph.json
# Waiting-on-you queue + deferred Notion writes carry personal context (upgrade P2, MR2-1);
# gitignored -> auto-covered by the encrypted vault backup (its set derives from this file)
system/human-actions.jsonl
system/pending-writes.jsonl
# ...and their BACKUP SIBLINGS (added 2026-07-28). A `.bak`/`.backup-*` copy of a gitignored personal
# file is just as personal, but the pattern above only names the exact filename, so the copy was NOT
# covered and one (`system/pending-writes.jsonl.bak`) was sitting STAGED for the nightly public push.
# This is the positive-space weakness of .gitignore on a PUBLIC repo: it protects only what it names,
# and a new sibling is unprotected by default until a human thinks of it.
system/*.jsonl.bak
system/*.jsonl.backup*
system/*.jsonl.bak-*
