# DEFAULT-DENY for project runtime state (2026-07-25, stress-test fix F-03). Every real personal-data
# leak on the public repo so far came from a work/NN/state/ dir that nobody remembered to gitignore
# BEFORE its first commit (the 07-20 CRM cadence.json + monday-list.md, real names + dating/family/
# recruiter context). The standing rule "gitignore-cover every new state/ dir first" was policy with no
# machine; this pattern IS the machine. Runtime state is regenerable and encrypted-backup-covered, so
# denying the whole class by default costs nothing and can never be forgotten again. If a specific state
# file is genuinely functional and safe to publish, un-ignore it explicitly with a reviewed `!` line.
work/*/state/

